  "comment": "kiln.vfx on the game client (enshrouded.exe 26430625 / svn 1287369). Evidence: docs/re/vfx.md section 4, docs/kiln/services/vfx.md. VfxCreateInstance(out, scene, &guid, &WorldTransform, &params) resolves the GUID in the VFX system's map (scene+scene.sys = VfxSystem; VfxResolve probes map.bits/map.keys, capacity map.cap, count map.count, slot = low 32 bits of the GUID & (cap-1), linear) and aborts on an unknown one: the guard detours it. The EcsFxController: FxUpdate(fxc, now, slotMask) is the update of the client program client_update_fx_controller (fxc+fxc.render = the renderer, render+render.holder+holder.scene = the VFX scene, fxc+fxc.world = the world); FxPlayAt(fxc, now, &guid, &WorldTransform 56 B, &params 72 B, &{i64 ns, bool has} 16 B) and FxPlayAttached(fxc, now, &guid, &attach 52 B {u32 entity, u8 slot, ecs::Offset 40 B at +8, u8 follow at +0x30}, &params, &timing) return a generation-checked FX handle; FxStop(fxc, &handle, now, &fade 16 B); FxLookup(fxc+fxc.pool, handle) -> entry or 0. An entry: u8 type at +0 (0 sound, 1 VFX), GUID +fx.guid, VFX instance +fx.vfx_handle, end time +fx.end_time with flag +fx.has_end, finish time +fx.finish_time with flag +fx.has_finish. FxStart(fxc, entry, now, &timing) with an empty GUID finishes the entry at once; a create that returns 0 retries every frame for ever, so the guard empties unknown GUIDs there. VfxSetParameter(scene, instance, nameHash, typeId, &{ptr, size}). The game has no finished signal, so Kiln stops a one-shot after the length its VfxResource gives: slot -> map.vals[slot] -> sys.vfx_table[value * 0xc0] + vfx_slot.resource = the VfxResource, with killTimeInSeconds at res.kill_time, the parameter descriptions (BlobArray of 12 B) at res.params and the default block at res.defaults.",
